      "time": "O(n²)",
      "space": "O(1)",
      "complexityWhy": "For each of the n numbers, the inner loop tries every number after it: about n²/2 sums. Nothing extra is stored.",
      "bottleneck": "Most pairs are checked even though one sum already tells you a lot about the others.",
      "insight": "If the numbers were sorted, one sum would tell you which way to go: too small, move the left end right; too big, move the right end left.",
      "code": {
        "python": "def twoSum(nums, target):\n    n = len(nums)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:\n                return [i, j]\n    return []"
